style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Key =
Status/Updates:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 4.0.3 has been through QA =
with a clean report and is likely to be =
released<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The CVE count for master rose =
sharply this week but a number of fixes were sent by Khem, =
thanks!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Bitbake changes in class =
handling merged which means classes can now be enforced to be in =
&#8220;global&#8221; or &#8220;recipe&#8221; scope. This handles a long =
standing usability issue of it not being clear which scope classes =
should be used in. For example, &#8220;testimage&#8221; now needs to be =
included via IMAGE_CLASSES and not via INHERIT. Global class inclusions =
in recipes such as &#8220;base&#8221; and &#8220;package&#8221; will now =
show a parsing error. &#8220;base&#8221; was particularly pointless and =
can simply be removed as it was always =
inherited.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The rust toolchain changes =
merged and are now being tested by default on the autobuilder but there =
is one intermittent issue with shebang length overflow in the SDK which =
still needs to be resolved<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We upgraded glibc to 2.36 and =
produced a new uninative version which supports =
this.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are patches out for =
review for the debug path improvements. These rely on a gcc patch and =
small change of gcc behavior which is being discussed with =
upstream.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There were cleanups to =
copyright and license headers in OE-Core and =
Bitbake.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&#8220;largefile&#8221; support =
in oe-core was cleaned up and removed as we assume this everywhere now, =
completing something we said would happen in release notes a few years =
ago.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Help is very much welcome in =
trying to resolve our autobuilder intermittent issues. You can see the =
list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
